The Freight Ledger Weekly
28 September 2026

Winter surcharges arrive early

Three road carriers on the routes into the Nordics have told customers that
winter surcharges will start on 1 November this year, a month earlier than
last. Fernway Logistics, which opens its northern service in January, says
it will not charge one in its first season.

Shippers we spoke to expect the early start to add between two and four
percent to northbound costs over the winter. Most say they will book space
for the spring now rather than wait for rates.

